       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is about twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day (2,000\u20132,550 mg depending on the formulation). A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCan you confirm what was intended? A few possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,000 mg twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day, a common regimen.\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- Some other dose that was mistyped.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please tell me the clinical rationale, and I'll add it as a note on the order."
      }
