       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I understand you're taking responsibility for it. But metformin has no added benefit above about 2,550 mg/day, and 5,100 mg/day mainly adds risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI effects. I can't enter a dose that has no plausible upside and a serious potential for harm, even with your confirmation.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum).\n- **Metformin 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day).\n- **Metformin 1,700 mg PO once daily or split into smaller doses**, if the total was meant to be lower.\n\nIf you think this patient needs more glycemic control than the maximum metformin dose gives, adding or adjusting a second agent such as insulin, a GLP-1 agonist, or an SGLT2 inhibitor would be safer. A pharmacist consult could also help. If you need to place the order as written, you can do it directly through your institution's process, which would include pharmacist review.\n\nTell me which option you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
